## Upstream research software

### EchoCLIP (Nature Medicine 2024)
- Christensen, Vukadinovic, Yuan, Ouyang.
- Code: https://github.com/echonet/echo_CLIP
- Hub weights: `hf-hub:mkaichristensen/echo-clip` (loaded at runtime; not vendored).
- Prompt strings in `echoclip/prompts.py` follow the published templates —
  attributed, not claimed as original clinical IP. Clean-room TA captions:
  `echoclip/prompts_ta.py`.
- `echoclip/text.py` is an independently authored report normalizer whose behavior
  intentionally overlaps upstream EchoCLIP report cleaning; no upstream code is
  vendored or line-copied in this repository, and whether the upstream
  echonet/echo_CLIP utils.py source was consulted is **unclear — needs author
  confirmation** (see `PROVENANCE.md`).

### EchoNet-Dynamic / Stanford AIMI
- Separate non-commercial terms: https://echonet.github.io/dynamic/
- Videos / `FileList` / `VolumeTracings` are NOT redistributed in this repository.

### CardiacCLIP (MICCAI 2025)
- https://github.com/xmed-lab/CardiacCLIP — external comparator only.
- Weights not bundled; see `echoclip/cardiacclip.py` download instructions.

